		"Kind": "youtube#playlistItem",
		"Snippet": {
			"ChannelId": "UCiZeuI-7OPs7TmMel6Q5Msw",
			"ChannelTitle": "Kanishk Nishar",
			"Description": "WARNING: The version performed here is the so called \u0022Soviet ending\u0022 which is an unofficial, louder alternative to the original quiet finale. Here the hushed closing pages (which traditionally feature an organ and signify Manfred\u0027s redemption and death) are omitted, and instead substituted by a fortissimo reprise of the main \u0022Manfred\u0022 theme from the end of the first movement.\n\nI did not have the full details of the concert in my notes, but with many thanks to http://www.youtube.com/@Gralsritter who has done some excellent detective work, I can now say that the performance was given  on 9th November 1995 in the  Th\u00E9\u00E2tre des Champs-\u00C9lys\u00E9es, Paris. The programme also included Miaskovsky Symphony no 25 which I am afraid I do not have. It was was not broadcast until 31 July 1996 in the UK.\n\nOrchestre National de France\nconducted by\nEvgeny Svetlanov\n\nFor more details see:\nhttps://genome.ch.bbc.co.uk/ef687766dde7470f817ec49fad6da723\n\nThis is part of a collection of live \u0022off air\u0022 recordings from radio broadcasts I have made since 1970, and I have recently preserved by transferring from tape to digital format. None of the recordings is derived from a commercial release, nor are they of commercial sound quality. No payment is sought for listening to these recordings, I am sharing them in the hope that they may give pleasure to other music lovers, as they have given pleasure to me. No copyright infringement is intended, please do contact me to allow me to correct the situation should this be the case.",
			"PlaylistId": "PL1zgNCoWt_7bdQf5RbldHEZHFyDkmOvJ4",
